      "Language": "pol",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Post-mortem studies of 50 cases of death in the course of recent myocardial infarction were made to analyse relations between coronary thrombosis and myocardial necrosis. We assessed and compared severity of necrotic changes in the myocardium in relation to thrombotic changes in the coronary vessels. Our results show an enhancement and evolution of thrombotic changes with time elapsing from the infarct completion and possible causal relations between a thrombus and infarct."},
